    <string name="orient_compass_info_title">What each number means</string>
    <string name="orient_compass_info_text">Signal: the strength of the cell you are on, in dBm. Closer to zero is stronger; −100 dBm or better counts as strong here.\n\nDirection: how far your heading is from the line to the target. Within 5° counts as lined up.\n\nGPS precision: how exact your position is, in metres. 15 m or better counts as precise. A bigger number means the phone is still guessing where you are.\n\nWhen all three are good at the same time, the spot is right for installing.</string>

